 "duration": 85.107,
 "sentences": [
  {
   "n": 1,
   "text": "A tiny splinter in your finger sets off your immune system.",
   "start": 0.0,
   "end": 3.193,
   "firstWord": 0
  },
  {
   "n": 2,
   "text": "Your skin is a wall that keeps germs out.",
   "start": 3.529,
   "end": 5.898,
   "firstWord": 11
  },
  {
   "n": 3,
   "text": "The splinter just punched a hole in it, and bacteria ride in on the wood.",
   "start": 6.235,
   "end": 10.275,
   "firstWord": 20
  },
  {
   "n": 4,
   "text": "Damaged cells release chemical signals.",
   "start": 10.728,
   "end": 13.293,
   "firstWord": 35
  },
  {
   "n": 5,
   "text": "Nearby blood vessels widen, so more blood flows in.",
   "start": 13.746,
   "end": 17.519,
   "firstWord": 40
  },
  {
   "n": 6,
   "text": "That's why the spot turns red, warm and swollen.",
   "start": 17.856,
   "end": 21.362,
   "firstWord": 49
  },
  {
   "n": 7,
   "text": "White blood cells squeeze out of the vessels and follow the signals.",
   "start": 21.699,
   "end": 25.298,
   "firstWord": 58
  },
  {
   "n": 8,
   "text": "Neutrophils usually arrive first and swallow bacteria whole.",
   "start": 25.751,
   "end": 29.988,
   "firstWord": 70
  },
  {
   "n": 9,
   "text": "Bigger cells called macrophages eat germs and clean up the mess.",
   "start": 30.441,
   "end": 34.807,
   "firstWord": 78
  },
  {
   "n": 10,
   "text": "Often, that's enough.",
   "start": 35.329,
   "end": 36.676,
   "firstWord": 89
  },
  {
   "n": 11,
   "text": "But a dendritic cell also grabs pieces of the germ and carries them to a lymph node, a small bean-shaped station.",
   "start": 37.07,
   "end": 44.408,
   "firstWord": 92
  },
  {
   "n": 12,
   "text": "There, the pieces are checked against a huge crowd of immune cells.",
   "start": 45.023,
   "end": 49.18,
   "firstWord": 113
  },
  {
   "n": 13,
   "text": "Only a few B cells fit this exact germ.",
   "start": 49.703,
   "end": 52.535,
   "firstWord": 125
  },
  {
   "n": 14,
   "text": "When one fits, it copies itself again and again.",
   "start": 52.988,
   "end": 56.285,
   "firstWord": 134
  },
  {
   "n": 15,
   "text": "The copies make antibodies, Y-shaped proteins that stick to this one germ.",
   "start": 56.808,
   "end": 62.218,
   "firstWord": 143
  },
  {
   "n": 16,
   "text": "Antibodies travel through the blood and coat the bacteria.",
   "start": 62.741,
   "end": 66.328,
   "firstWord": 155
  },
  {
   "n": 17,
   "text": "A coated germ is easier for the eating cells to find.",
   "start": 66.85,
   "end": 69.776,
   "firstWord": 164
  },
  {
   "n": 18,
   "text": "The first time, this takes days.",
   "start": 70.229,
   "end": 72.063,
   "firstWord": 175
  },
  {
   "n": 19,
   "text": "But some B cells stay behind as memory cells.",
   "start": 72.4,
   "end": 75.163,
   "firstWord": 181
  },
  {
   "n": 20,
   "text": "If the same germ comes back, the response is faster and stronger.",
   "start": 75.686,
   "end": 79.087,
   "firstWord": 190
  },
  {
   "n": 21,
   "text": "That's the idea behind vaccines.",
   "start": 79.54,
   "end": 81.397,
   "firstWord": 202
  },
  {
   "n": 22,
   "text": "Back at your finger, the fight is over, and the wall is whole again.",
   "start": 81.548,
   "end": 85.078,
   "firstWord": 207
  }
 ],
